==English==
===Etymology===
Portmanteau of [[red]] + [[neck]] (referring to the the sunburn on the neck typical of rural form workers) 
===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#{{context|slang}} An uneducated, unsophisticated, or poor white person, typically used to describe residents of the [[rural]] Southern US.
#{{rfv-sense}}A [[blue-collar]] worker who bucks the system and refuses to give in to political correctness.

